History                                                             39 1451
----------                                                          39 1451
                                                                    39 1451
This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics     39 1451
(LEIP) group at North Carolina State University.  One temperature   39 1451
(300 K) is available in this library.  The inelastic scattering     39 1451
cross section libraries for C5O2H8 (Lucite) were developed using    39 1451
molecular dynamics methods [1]. This material is a polymer. The     39 1451
incoherent elastic cross section is significant, so the MT = 2      39 1451
section for elastic scattering is present. The LEAPR module from    39 1451
NJOY code system was used to produce MT = 2 and MT = 4 data. By     39 1451
convention, MAT=39 and ZA=139 are used for H in Lucite.             39 1451
                                                                    39 1451
 References                                                         39 1451
 ----------                                                         39 1451
                                                                    39 1451
 1. A.I. Hawari, "Modern Techniques in Inelastic Thermal Neutron    39 1451
    Scattering Analysis," Nuclear Data Sheets 118 (2014) 172.       39 1451
